IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P7-gates`

-- P7-governance: Articles 64 to 70 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- Chapter VII, governance: the AI Office, the European Artificial Intelligence Board, the advisory forum, the scientific panel of independent experts,
-- and the national competent authorities. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`:
-- Chapter VII applies from 2 August 2025 (Art 113(b)), before the Omnibus came into force on 27 July 2026, so the as-enacted text governed from 2 August 2025
-- to 26 July 2026 and the amended text governs from 27 July 2026. Provisions the Omnibus changed (Art 64(3) inserted, Art 69(2), Art 70(8)) are encoded in both versions
-- and their dispatchers are tested on both sides of 27 July 2026.
-- Much of this Chapter addresses officials only (the Commission, the Board, the AI Office, the Member States): it is encoded here, and gives the seats little.
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 65(2) participant` IS ONE OF
    `Art 65(2) a representative of a Member State`
    `Art 65(2) the European Data Protection Supervisor`
    `Art 65(2) the AI Office`
    `Art 65(2) another national or Union authority, body or expert`

DECLARE `Art 65(2) place in the Board's meetings` IS ONE OF
    `Art 65(2) member of the Board`
    `Art 65(2) observer`
    `Art 65(2) attends the meetings without taking part in the votes`
    `Art 65(2) invited to the meetings by the Board case by case`

§ `Article 64: the AI Office`

-- src:1004 | 1. The Commission shall develop Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office.
@ref Art 64(1) (src:1004)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission develops Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 64(1) the Commission has developed Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission develops Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall develop Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office"

-- src:1005 | 2. Member States shall facilitate the tasks entrusted to the AI Office, as reflected in this Regulation.
@ref Art 64(2) (src:1005)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Member States facilitate the tasks entrusted to the AI Office, as reflected in this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 64(2) the Member States have facilitated the tasks entrusted to the AI Office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member States facilitate the tasks entrusted to the AI Office, as reflected in this Regulation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States shall facilitate the tasks entrusted to the AI Office, as reflected in this Regulation"

-- src:1007 | 3. Without prejudice to the budgetary procedure, the AI Office shall be allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation.
@ref Art 64(3) as amended (src:1007)
GIVEN `the AI Office is allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 64(3) as amended the AI Office has been allocated adequate resources` MEANS
    BRANCH
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the AI Office is allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Without prejudice to the budgetary procedure, the AI Office shall be allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation"

-- src:1007 | 3. Without prejudice to the budgetary procedure, the AI Office shall be allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation.
@ref Art 64(3) (dispatcher: gate, then the version in force) (src:1007)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI Office is allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 64(3) the AI Office has been allocated adequate resources` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN NOTHING  -- VERSION as enacted. NOTHING-kind (silent): the enacted Article 64 has two paragraphs; it says nothing about the resources of the AI Office
         WHEN `as amended` THEN `Art 64(3) as amended the AI Office has been allocated adequate resources` `the AI Office is allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation`  -- VERSION as amended

-- src:1007 | 3. Without prejudice to the budgetary procedure, the AI Office shall be allocated adequate resources to effectively perform its duties and exercise its powers in relation to the enforcement of this Regulation.
@ref Art 64(3) without prejudice to the budgetary procedure (src:1007)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the procedure is the budgetary procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 64(3) the allocation of resources prejudices the budgetary procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the procedure is the budgetary procedure` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Without prejudice to the budgetary procedure"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

§ `Article 65: the European Artificial Intelligence Board`

-- src:1011 | 1. A European Artificial Intelligence Board (the ‘Board’) is hereby established.
@ref Art 65(1) (the Board is established) (src:1011)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 65(1) the European Artificial Intelligence Board is established on the date asked` MEANS
    IF `Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE  -- "A European Artificial Intelligence Board (the 'Board') is hereby established": from the day Chapter VII applies
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives

-- src:1012 | 2. The Board shall be composed of one representative per Member State. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall participate as observer. The AI Office shall also attend the Board’s meetings, without taking part in the votes. Other national and Union authorities, bodies or experts may be invited to the meetings by the Board on a case by case basis, where the issues discussed are of relevance for them.
@ref Art 65(2) (the place of each participant in the Board's meetings) (src:1012)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the participant` IS A `Art 65(2) participant`
      `the issues discussed are of relevance for the participant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 65(2) place in the Board's meetings`
`Art 65(2) the participant's place in the Board's meetings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `the participant`
         WHEN `Art 65(2) a representative of a Member State` THEN JUST `Art 65(2) member of the Board`  -- "composed of one representative per Member State"
         WHEN `Art 65(2) the European Data Protection Supervisor` THEN JUST `Art 65(2) observer`  -- "shall participate as observer"
         WHEN `Art 65(2) the AI Office` THEN JUST `Art 65(2) attends the meetings without taking part in the votes`  -- "shall also attend the Board's meetings, without taking part in the votes"
         WHEN `Art 65(2) another national or Union authority, body or expert` THEN IF `the issues discussed are of relevance for the participant` THEN JUST `Art 65(2) invited to the meetings by the Board case by case` ELSE NOTHING  -- the grant: "may be invited ... where the issues discussed are of relevance for them". NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the issues discussed are of relevance for them"

-- src:1013 | 3. Each representative shall be designated by their Member State for a period of three years, renewable once.
@ref Art 65(3) (the three years of the designation) (src:1013)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the Member State designated the representative` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 65(3) the date on which the designation of the representative ends` MEANS
    IF `Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST (`add years` `the date on which the Member State designated the representative` 3)  -- "designated by their Member State for a period of three years"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives

-- src:1013 | 3. Each representative shall be designated by their Member State for a period of three years, renewable once.
@ref Art 65(3) (renewable once) (src:1013)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of times the designation has already been renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 65(3) the designation of the representative may be renewed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the number of times the designation has already been renewed` LESS THAN 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "renewable once"

