`Art 66(e) the matters on which the Board may issue recommendations and written opinions` MEANS
    LIST
        "on the development and application of codes of conduct and codes of practice pursuant to this Regulation, as well as of the Commission’s guidelines"
      , "the evaluation and review of this Regulation pursuant to Article 112, including as regards the serious incident reports referred to in Article 73, and the functioning of the EU database referred to in Article 71, the preparation of the delegated or implementing acts, and as regards possible alignments of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I"
      , "on technical specifications or existing standards regarding the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2"
      , "on the use of harmonised standards or common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41"
      , "trends, such as European global competitiveness in AI, the uptake of AI in the Union, and the development of digital skills"
      , "trends on the evolving typology of AI value chains, in particular on the resulting implications in terms of accountability"
      , "on the potential need for amendment to Annex III in accordance with Article 7, and on the potential need for possible revision of Article 5 pursuant to Article 112, taking into account relevant available evidence and the latest developments in technology"

@ref Art 66(e)(i) to (vii) (the matters on which the Board may issue recommendations and written opinions) (src:1032-1038; membership)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 66(e) the matter is one on which the Board may issue recommendations and written opinions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF elem `the matter` `Art 66(e) the matters on which the Board may issue recommendations and written opinions` THEN JUST TRUE  -- "including"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names these and does not say that others are excluded

-- src:1041 | (h) cooperate, as appropriate, with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, as well as relevant Union expert groups and networks, in particular in the fields of product safety, cybersecurity, competition, digital and media services, financial services, consumer protection, data and fundamental rights protection;
@ref Art 66(h) (src:1041)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `it is appropriate to cooperate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board cooperates with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, as well as relevant Union expert groups and networks, in particular in the fields of product safety, cybersecurity, competition, digital and media services, financial services, consumer protection, data and fundamental rights protection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 66(h) the Board may cooperate with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies and with relevant Union expert groups and networks` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`it is appropriate to cooperate`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as appropriate"
        IF `the Board cooperates with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, as well as relevant Union expert groups and networks, in particular in the fields of product safety, cybersecurity, competition, digital and media services, financial services, consumer protection, data and fundamental rights protection` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the grant: "cooperate, as appropriate, with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, as well as relevant Union expert groups and networks"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the case falls outside what the grant names

§ `Article 67: the advisory forum`

-- src:1051 | 1. An advisory forum shall be established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission, and to contribute to their tasks under this Regulation.
@ref Art 67(1) (src:1051)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `an advisory forum is established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission, and to contribute to their tasks under this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(1) an advisory forum has been established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`an advisory forum is established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission, and to contribute to their tasks under this Regulation`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An advisory forum shall be established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission, and to contribute to their tasks under this Regulation"

-- src:1052 | 2. The membership of the advisory forum shall represent a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia. The membership of the advisory forum shall be balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests and, within the category of commercial interests, with regard to SMEs and other undertakings.
@ref Art 67(2) first sentence (src:1052)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the membership represents a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(2) the membership of the advisory forum represents a balanced selection of stakeholders` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the membership represents a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The membership of the advisory forum shall represent a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia"

-- src:1052 | 2. The membership of the advisory forum shall represent a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia. The membership of the advisory forum shall be balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests and, within the category of commercial interests, with regard to SMEs and other undertakings.
@ref Art 67(2) second sentence (src:1052)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the membership is balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within the category of commercial interests, the membership is balanced with regard to SMEs and other undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(2) the membership of the advisory forum is balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests and to SMEs and other undertakings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the membership is balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests` AND `within the category of commercial interests, the membership is balanced with regard to SMEs and other undertakings`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The membership of the advisory forum shall be balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests and, within the category of commercial interests, with regard to SMEs and other undertakings"

-- src:1053 | 3. The Commission shall appoint the members of the advisory forum, in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2, from amongst stakeholders with recognised expertise in the field of AI.
@ref Art 67(3) (src:1053)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Commission appoints the members of the advisory forum in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members are from amongst stakeholders with recognised expertise in the field of AI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(3) the Commission has appointed the members of the advisory forum in accordance with the criteria of paragraph 2` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Commission appoints the members of the advisory forum in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2` AND `the members are from amongst stakeholders with recognised expertise in the field of AI`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commission shall appoint the members of the advisory forum, in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2, from amongst stakeholders with recognised expertise in the field of AI"

-- src:1054 | 4. The term of office of the members of the advisory forum shall be two years, which may be extended by up to no more than four years.
@ref Art 67(4) (the term of office of two years) (src:1054)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the member took office` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 67(4) the date on which the term of office of the member ends` MEANS
    IF `Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`
    THEN JUST (`add years` `the date on which the member took office` 2)  -- "The term of office of the members of the advisory forum shall be two years"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives

-- src:1054 | 4. The term of office of the members of the advisory forum shall be two years, which may be extended by up to no more than four years.
@ref Art 67(4) (the extension of up to no more than four years) (src:1054)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of years by which the term of office is extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(4) the extension of the term of office is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the number of years by which the term of office is extended` AT MOST 4)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which may be extended by up to no more than four years" (the extension, not the whole term: fork F-67-4)

-- src:1055 | 5. The Fundamental Rights Agency, ENISA, the European Committee for Standardization (CEN), the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC), and the European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI) shall be permanent members of the advisory forum.
@ref Art 67(5) (the permanent members of the advisory forum) (src:1055; the list)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Art 67(5) the permanent members of the advisory forum` MEANS
    LIST
        "the Fundamental Rights Agency"
      , "ENISA"
      , "the European Committee for Standardization (CEN)"
      , "the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC)"
      , "the European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI)"

@ref Art 67(5) (the permanent members of the advisory forum) (src:1055; membership)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the body` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(5) the body is a permanent member of the advisory forum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF elem `the body` `Art 67(5) the permanent members of the advisory forum` THEN JUST TRUE  -- "shall be permanent members of the advisory forum"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names five permanent members and does not say that another body may not be a (non-permanent) member

-- src:1056 | 6. The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure. It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2. The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once.
@ref Art 67(6) first sentence (src:1056)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the advisory forum draws up its rules of procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(6) the advisory forum has drawn up its rules of procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the advisory forum draws up its rules of procedure`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure"

-- src:1056 | 6. The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure. It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2. The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once.
@ref Art 67(6) second sentence (src:1056)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the advisory forum elects two co-chairs from among its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election is in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 67(6) the advisory forum has elected two co-chairs from among its members` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII (group of Section 4, Chapters V, VII, XII and Art 78) applies from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the advisory forum elects two co-chairs from among its members` AND `the election is in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2"

-- src:1056 | 6. The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure. It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2. The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once.
@ref Art 67(6) third sentence (the term of office of the co-chairs: two years, renewable once) (src:1056)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the co-chair took office` IS A DATE
      `the number of times the term of office has already been renewed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 67(6) the date on which the term of office of the co-chair ends` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 64 the group of Chapter VII applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VII applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the number of times the term of office has already been renewed` LESS THAN 2 THEN JUST (`add years` `the date on which the co-chair took office` 2)  -- "The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once": each term lasts two years
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text allows one renewal; a term after two terms is not described

-- src:1056 | 6. The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure. It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2. The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once.
